Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:39:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] perf(media): serve HTTP Range requests with a partial
 object-storage GET

Review #20: GET /api/chat/media/{id}/file read the whole object from
SeaweedFS and sliced it in Python for every Range request, so each seek in
a long video was a full download on the app side (memory and time).
object_storage_service.get_object_range() passes the client's byte range
to S3 and parses Content-Range; the handler answers 206 from that window,
416 on InvalidRange (Content-Range: */size) and only falls back to the full
read for multi-range/malformed specs or non-media kinds, as before.

Tests: tests/test_video_media_policy.py::test_range_request_fetches_only_the_window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
